#! mathcas 2 notebook

#% title
# zernike_r

#% text
# `zernike_r(n, m, r)` gives the radial Zernike polynomial R_n^m(r).

#% section
# Details

#% item
# R_n^m is zero when n - m is odd or |m| > n.

#% section
# Examples

#% subsection
# Basic examples

#% cell
zernike_r(4, 2, r)
#% output
#= -3*r^2 + 4*r^4

#% cell
zernike_r(3, 1, 0.5)
#% output
#= -0.625

